  1| //! Automatic Git checkpoints for an agent's private filesystem workspace.
  2| //!
  3| //! The feature is deliberately a tool decorator: file tools, patches, shell
  4| //! redirects, downloads, and future workspace-writing tools all pass the same
  5| //! after-call boundary. A call that changed nothing produces no commit, and a
  6| //! Git failure is logged without replacing the tool's real result.
  7| //!
  8| //! History is permanent for the lifetime of the out-of-band repository: a
  9| //! workspace file committed at one checkpoint and deleted later survives in
 10| //! `workspace.git` objects, so operators who enable checkpoints on workspaces
 11| //! that can hold secrets must rotate or purge history deliberately (see the
 12| //! retention note in `docs/spec/runtime/workspace-layout.md`).
